    "intro_html":  "Japchae is the Korean party dish, sweet potato glass noodles tossed with vegetables in sesame and soy until every strand goes glossy. Those noodles are called dangmyeon and they are the reason this holds up in a container: they stay chewy and springy for days instead of going mushy the way wheat noodles do. We add turkey to turn a side dish into dinner, at \u003cstrong\u003e591 calories and 29 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.19\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
